<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege tower</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as siege towers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A siege tower is a mobile wooden tower used to bring attackers to the top of fortification walls. It was used from ancient times across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> profile notes that Assyrian engineers developed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battering-ram">battering rams</a>, siege towers and undermining techniques to capture fortified cities.</p></div>
